{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1787425814146,"sessionID":"ses_fd51eaec7ffehwG0fu6RiLBPJO","part":{"id":"prt_02ae1767a001w35JF10b7Hg6LQ","messageID":"msg_02ae1736f002XJr3mQYG0Qp2sL","sessionID":"ses_fd51eaec7ffehwG0fu6RiLBPJO","snapshot":"1c0ca0d1e9c3dcc89d775605d8a1753593c2a309","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1787425818122,"sessionID":"ses_fd51eaec7ffehwG0fu6RiLBPJO","part":{"id":"prt_02ae1772a001zfDtiPYYmpr0sD","messageID":"msg_02ae1736f002XJr3mQYG0Qp2sL","sessionID":"ses_fd51eaec7ffehwG0fu6RiLBPJO","type":"text","text":"## Architecture\n\nThis repository is a **coding-assistant benchmarking study**. It has two halves: an interactive study-plan website and a reproducible harness for running coding assistants (Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode, Pi) against frozen tasks.\n\n- **`app/`** — the Next.js study-plan site. `app/page.tsx` is a single client component holding all content (assistant cards, model table, lanes, tasks, scoring, stages) plus localStorage-based progress tracking. `app/layout.tsx` sets metadata and fonts; `app/globals.css` holds styling.\n- **`worker/index.ts`** — the Cloudflare Worker entry point. It intercepts `/_vinext/image` for image optimization, otherwise delegates to the vinext app-router handler.\n- **`db/`** — Drizzle setup. `db/schema.ts` is intentionally empty; `db/index.ts` exposes `getDb()` for a D1 binding. The site currently uses no database.\n- **`benchmark/`** — the frozen research contract. `STUDY.md` defines lanes, score, and stop rules; `tasks/T1-repo-map/` holds the versioned task (`task.json`, `prompt.md`, `rubric.json`); `schemas/` holds JSON Schemas; `runs/` stores generated evidence.\n- **`scripts/`** — the harness: `benchmark-env.mjs` (environment snapshot), `benchmark-validate.mjs` (contract checks), `benchmark-run.mjs` (executes a run and records artifacts).\n- **`tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`** — server-render smoke test.\n\nStack: Next.js 16 + React 19, Vite 8, Tailwind 4, Cloudflare Workers via `vinext`, Drizzle ORM, Node 22.\n\n## Main request flow\n\nA browser request to `/` hits the Cloudflare Worker (`worker/index.ts:29`). The path is not `/_vinext/image`, so it calls `handler.fetch` from `vinext/server/app-router-entry` (`worker/index.ts:43`), which renders the Next app. `app/layout.tsx` wraps the page; `app/page.tsx` (a `\"use client\"` component) renders the full study plan. On mount, `useEffect` reads `assistant-study-progress` from `localStorage` (`app/page.tsx:393-410`) to restore checked stages; toggling a stage writes back to storage (`app/page.tsx:419-432`). The server-rendered HTML is returned to the browser. The test at `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs:25` exercises this same path by importing the built worker and calling `fetch`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run typecheck` — `tsc --noEmit`; proves TypeScript types are consistent.\n- `npm run lint` — ESLint over the repo (ignoring `dist`/`.next`); proves style/rule compliance.\n- `npm test` — builds then runs `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`; proves the site server-renders with expected content and no forbidden markers.\n- `npm run verify` — runs typecheck, lint, test, and `benchmark:validate` together.\n- `npm run benchmark:validate` — checks task/run/result schemas, the T1 task contract, rubric sums to 100, and that `CLAUDE.md` imports `@AGENTS.md`.\n- `npm run benchmark:env` — snapshots hardware, tool versions, and git state (read-only unless `--write`).\n- `npm run benchmark:run` — previews or executes a recorded run.\n\n## Risks and unknowns\n\n- **Evidence:** `db/schema.ts` is empty and `db/index.ts` throws without a D1 binding, yet `worker/index.ts` declares `DB: D1Database` and `drizzle.config.ts` exists. **Inference:** the DB layer is scaffolding; the site does not use it, so a future feature touching persistence has no established pattern.\n- **Evidence:** `app/page.tsx` is a 1123-line single component with all data hardcoded as module constants. **Inference:** adding a \"pilot completed\" status means editing this one file; there is no data layer or componentization to reuse, so the file will keep growing.\n- **Evidence:** `benchmark-run.mjs` snapshots the whole repo and auto-fails read-only runs on any change (`scripts/benchmark-run.mjs:255-257`), and `benchmark/runs/` is git-ignored. **Inference:** the harness is sensitive to workspace state; running it from a dirty tree or with build artifacts present could produce false failures, and there is no CI wiring the benchmark into `verify`.\n\n## Small change plan\n\nAdd a visible \"pilot completed\" status to the study page:\n\n1. **Add state/data** in `app/page.tsx`: a `pilotCompleted` boolean (default `false`), initialized from `localStorage` in the existing `useEffect`, with a toggle handler mirroring `toggleStage`.\n2. **Render the status** in the header `mini-progress` area or the `#steps` section (`app/page.tsx:455-460`, `952-994`), showing a badge/label when `pilotCompleted` is true.\n3. **Persist** the flag to `localStorage` (e.g. key `assistant-study-pilot`) in the toggle handler, wrapped in the same try/catch used elsewhere.\n4. **Verify** with `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint`, then `npm test` to confirm the server-rendered HTML still passes; optionally add an assertion in `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs` for the new marker.\n5. **Manual check** via `npm run dev` to confirm the badge appears, toggles, and survives a reload.\n\nNo files were modified; all claims above are from files I inspected.","time":{"start":1787425814314,"end":1787425818119}}}
